  "interpretation": "Two independent rises accompany the vendor-named fan-temperature-level field0->1; it returns to0 before RPM fully decays. Table remains2, barometric level0, tray status1, n2h status0x0f00; n2h/h2n override fields remain0. Inlet/working values move27->28 and CPU37->38 around rises, but these co-vary, so the actual selected sensor/threshold and hysteresis are not isolated. This supports controller temperature-band cycling; it does not establish a defective policy, prove PSU causality, or validate a tuning write. Alarm Normal is distinct from these control bands.",
